---
description: Minitest asserts observable outcomes, never implementation
alwaysApply: true
---

# Test outcomes, not implementation

A test is a scenario: actor, starting point, action, expected observable outcome. That is the [Minitest Rails](https://minitestrails.com/guide/how-to-approach-testing) standard. Model tests cover [validations, scopes, and methods](https://minitestrails.com/guide/testing-models). HTTP tests cover status, redirects, and copied page text.

Outcomes include validation errors, persisted records, scope results, HTTP status, redirects, and copied page text. Not grepping Gemfile, migrations, routes, or test_helper. Not asserting `enum.keys` lists, `column_names`, or Turbo/HTML internals.

Cursor `.mdc` rules are agent process guardrails. They are not proved by source-grep Minitest.

```ruby
# bad
assert_equal %w[pricing refunds], Model.categories.keys
assert_match(/create_table :foo/, File.read("db/migrate/..."))
```

```ruby
# good
refute document.valid?
assert_includes document.errors[:category], "is not included in the list"

get customers_path
assert_select "a", text: "Acme Corp"
```
